.TH SERVAL-SETUP 8 "" "Serval" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
serval-setup \- configure Serval's web listener, TLS certificate and host-admin group
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B serval-setup status
.br
.B serval-setup admin-group
.I group
.br
.B serval-setup listen \-\-loopback
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR port ]
.br
.B serval-setup listen \-\-address
.I ip
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR port ]
.B \-\-tls self-signed \-\-hostname
.I name[,name...]
.br
.B serval-setup listen \-\-address
.I ip
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR port ]
.B \-\-tls custom \-\-certificate
.I file
.B \-\-key
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B serval-setup
is a local administration tool that only root can run. It is not reachable through
the Serval web application or the Agent socket, and it never passes an argument to a shell.
.PP
After installation Serval's web application listens only on
.B http://127.0.0.1:9080
(reach it through an SSH tunnel). Exposing it to the network is a deliberate step:
any non-loopback address requires TLS.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the listener, TLS mode, certificate subject names, expiry and SHA-256 fingerprint,
the host-admin group and the state of both services. Private key material is never printed.
.TP
.BI admin-group " group"
Change the host-admin group. The group must exist, must match Serval's group name grammar
and must not have GID 0. The Agent configuration is rewritten atomically (other settings such as
.B idleMinutes
are kept) and the Agent and then the web application are restarted.
.TP
.B listen
Set the web listener. A literal IPv4 or IPv6 address and a port from 1024 to 65535 are required
because the web application runs without privileges. The web application is restarted. If it does
not become active, the previous files are restored, it is restarted again and the command fails.
.SH LISTEN OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-loopback
Return to the default: loopback only, plain HTTP, TLS files removed. Only
.B \-\-port
may be combined with it.
.TP
.BI \-\-address " ip"
Address to listen on, for example
.B 0.0.0.0
or
.BR :: .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
Port, 1024 to 65535. Defaults to 9443 with TLS and 9080 without.
.TP
.BI \-\-tls " self-signed" | custom
.B self-signed
generates an ECDSA P-256 certificate valid for 365 days for the names given with
.BR \-\-hostname ;
the SHA-256 fingerprint is printed so that it can be verified out of band.
.B custom
validates and copies an operator certificate chain and unencrypted private key.
.TP
.BI \-\-hostname " names"
Comma-separated DNS names or IP addresses (at most 10) for the certificate.
.TP
.BI \-\-certificate " file" ", " \-\-key " file"
PEM certificate chain and matching unencrypted key. Both must be regular files given by an absolute path
without symbolic links, and the certificate must not be expired.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/serval/web.json
Listener settings (root:serval-web, mode 0640).
.TP
.I /etc/serval/tls/cert.pem
Certificate (root, mode 0644).
.TP
.I /etc/serval/tls/key.pem
Private key (root:serval-web, mode 0640).
.TP
.I /etc/serval/agent.json
Agent configuration including the host-admin group (root, mode 0600).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
serval-setup listen \-\-address 0.0.0.0 \-\-port 8443 \-\-tls self-signed \-\-hostname admin.example.test
serval-setup listen \-\-address 192.0.2.10 \-\-tls custom \-\-certificate /root/serval.pem \-\-key /root/serval.key
serval-setup listen \-\-loopback
serval-setup admin-group serval-admins
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; non-zero when the arguments are invalid, a validation fails or a change had to be rolled back.
Invalid arguments change nothing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dpkg-reconfigure (8)
